{"id":"mahabharata-5-176","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":176,"title":"षट्सप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 176 · Amba asks Parashurama to slay Bhishma","summary":{"en":"Akritavrana asks whether Amba wants revenge on Shalva or on Bhishma, and she chooses Bhishma as the cause of her suffering. Parashurama arrives, hears her, and when she refuses to return to Shalva, she begs him to kill Bhishma.","kn":"ಶಾಲ್ವನ ಮೇಲೋ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಮೇಲೋ ಪ್ರತೀಕಾರ ಬೇಕೆಂದು ಅಕೃತವ್ರಣನು ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ ಅಂಬೆ ತನ್ನ ದುಃಖಕ್ಕೆ ಕಾರಣನಾದ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಆರಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಪರಶುರಾಮನು ಬಂದು ಅವಳ ಮಾತು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶಾಲ್ವನ ಬಳಿ ಮರಳಲು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲೆಂದು ಅವಳು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"अकृतव्रण पूछते हैं कि अम्बा शाल्व से प्रतिशोध चाहती है या भीष्म से, और वह अपने दुःख के कारण भीष्म को चुनती है। परशुराम आकर उसकी बात सुनते हैं, और शाल्व के पास लौटने से मना कर वह उनसे भीष्म को मारने की विनती करती है।","te":"శాల్వునిపై ప్రతీకారమా భీష్మునిపైనా అని అకృతవ్రణుడు అడగగా అంబ తన దుఃఖానికి కారణమైన భీష్ముని ఎంచుకుంటుంది. పరశురాముడు వచ్చి ఆమె మాట వింటాడు; శాల్వుని దగ్గరకు తిరిగివెళ్లడానికి నిరాకరించి భీష్ముని చంపమని ఆమె వేడుకుంటుంది.","ta":"ஶால்வன் மீதா பீஷ்மர் மீதா பழிவாங்க வேண்டும் என்று அக்ருதவ்ரணர் கேட்க, தன் துன்பத்துக்குக் காரணமான பீஷ்மரை அம்பை தேர்கிறாள். பரஶுராமர் வந்து அவள் சொல்லைக் கேட்க, ஶால்வனிடம் திரும்ப மறுத்து பீஷ்மரைக் கொல்லுமாறு அவள் வேண்டுகிறாள்.","ml":"അംബ ശാല്വനോടാണോ ഭീഷ്മരോടാണോ പ്രതികാരം ചെയ്യേണ്ടതെന്ന് അകൃതവ്രണൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; തന്റെ ദുരിതത്തിന്റെ കാരണം ഭീഷ്മരാണെന്ന് അവൾ തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കുന്നു. പരശുരാമൻ എത്തി അവളുടെ കഥ കേൾക്കുന്നു; ശാല്വന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് മടങ്ങാൻ അവൾ വിസമ്മതിക്കുമ്പോൾ, ഭീഷ്മരെ കൊല്ലണമെന്ന് അവൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് യാചിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.176; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"अकृतव्रण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दुःखद्वयमिदं भद्रे कतरस्य चिकीर्षसि ।\nप्रतिकर्तव्यमबले तत्त्वं वत्से ब्रवीहि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are two sorrows here, good lady; for which do you wish a remedy? Tell me truly, weak one, my child."}},{"n":2,"text":"यदि सौभपतिर्भद्रे नियोक्तव्यो मते तव ।\nनियोक्ष्यति महात्मा तं रामस्त्वद्धितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, in your view, the king of Saubha is to be urged, the great-souled Rama will urge him, wishing your good."}},{"n":3,"text":"अथापगेयं भीष्मं तं रामेणेच्छसि धीमता ।\nरणे विनिर्जितं द्रष्टुं कुर्यात्तदपि भार्गवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if you wish to see Ganga's son Bhishma defeated in battle by the wise Rama, the Bhargava will do that too."}},{"n":4,"text":"सृञ्जयस्य वचः श्रुत्वा तव चैव शुचिस्मिते ।\nयदत्रानन्तरं कार्यं तदद्यैव विचिन्त्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard the Srinjaya's words and yours, fair-smiling one, think today what the next thing to be done is."}},{"text":"अम्बोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Amba said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अपनीतास्मि भीष्मेण भगवन्नविजानता ।\nन हि जानाति मे भीष्मो ब्रह्मञ्शाल्वगतं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Revered one, I was carried off by Bhishma, who did not know; Bhishma did not know, Brahmin, that my heart was set on Shalva."}},{"n":6,"text":"एतद्विचार्य मनसा भवानेव विनिश्चयम् ।\nविचिनोतु यथान्यायं विधानं क्रियतां तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Considering this in your mind, you yourself decide, and let the remedy be made in a proper way."}},{"n":7,"text":"भीष्मे वा कुरुशार्दूले शाल्वराजेऽथ वा पुनः ।\nउभयोरेव वा ब्रह्मन्यद्युक्तं तत्समाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether it be against Bhishma, tiger of the Kurus, or the king of Shalva, or both, Brahmin, do what is fitting."}},{"n":8,"text":"निवेदितं मया ह्येतद्दुःखमूलं यथातथम् ।\nविधानं तत्र भगवन्कर्तुमर्हसि युक्तितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you truly the root of this sorrow; you should arrange the remedy, sir, by reason."}},{"text":"अकृतव्रण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"उपपन्नमिदं भद्रे यदेवं वरवर्णिनि ।\nधर्मं प्रति वचो ब्रूयाः शृणु चेदं वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is fitting, good lady, that you speak so, fair one, about dharma; hear these words of mine too."}},{"n":10,"text":"यदि त्वामापगेयो वै न नयेद्गजसाह्वयम् ।\nशाल्वस्त्वां शिरसा भीरु गृह्णीयाद्रामचोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If Ganga's son had not taken you to Hastinapura, timid one, Shalva, urged by Rama, would have taken you on his head."}},{"n":11,"text":"तेन त्वं निर्जिता भद्रे यस्मान्नीतासि भामिनि ।\nसंशयः शाल्वराजस्य तेन त्वयि सुमध्यमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But because you were won and carried off by him, good lady, the king of Shalva has doubt about you, slender one."}},{"n":12,"text":"भीष्मः पुरुषमानी च जितकाशी तथैव च ।\nतस्मात्प्रतिक्रिया युक्ता भीष्मे कारयितुं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma thinks himself a man and is proud of his conquest; so it is right for you to have vengeance done against Bhishma."}},{"text":"अम्बोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Amba said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"ममाप्येष महान्ब्रह्मन्हृदि कामोऽभिवर्तते ।\nघातयेयं यदि रणे भीष्ममित्येव नित्यदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great desire, Brahmin, has been growing in my heart too, always: that I might have Bhishma killed in battle."}},{"n":14,"text":"भीष्मं वा शाल्वराजं वा यं वा दोषेण गच्छसि ।\nप्रशाधि तं महाबाहो यत्कृतेऽहं सुदुःखिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether Bhishma or the king of Shalva, whichever you find at fault, mighty-armed one, punish him, for whose sake I am so greatly afflicted."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"एवं कथयतामेव तेषां स दिवसो गतः ।\nरात्रिश्च भरतश्रेष्ठ सुखशीतोष्णमारुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they were speaking thus, that day passed, best of Bharatas, and the night came, with a pleasant mix of cool and warm breezes."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो रामः प्रादुरासीत्प्रज्वलन्निव तेजसा ।\nशिष्यैः परिवृतो राजञ्जटाचीरधरो मुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama appeared, blazing as if with energy, surrounded by his disciples, king, the sage wearing matted hair and bark."}},{"n":17,"text":"धनुष्पाणिरदीनात्मा खड्गं बिभ्रत्परश्वधी ।\nविरजा राजशार्दूल सोऽभ्ययात्सृञ्जयं नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bow in hand, of undaunted spirit, carrying a sword and axe, free of passion, tiger among kings, he approached King Srinjaya."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततस्तं तापसा दृष्ट्वा स च राजा महातपाः ।\nतस्थुः प्राञ्जलयः सर्वे सा च कन्या तपस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, the ascetics, the king of great austerity and the ascetic maiden all stood with folded hands."}},{"n":19,"text":"पूजयामासुरव्यग्रा मधुपर्केण भार्गवम् ।\nअर्चितश्च यथायोगं निषसाद सहैव तैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They calmly honored the Bhargava with the honey-offering, and having been honored duly he sat with them."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः पूर्वव्यतीतानि कथयेते स्म तावुभौ ।\nसृञ्जयश्च स राजर्षिर्जामदग्न्यश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Srinjaya the royal sage and Jamadagni's son told each other tales of times gone by, Bharata."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः कथान्ते राजर्षिर्भृगुश्रेष्ठं महाबलम् ।\nउवाच मधुरं काले रामं वचनमर्थवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the tales the royal sage said to the strong chief of the Bhrigus, at the right time, sweet and meaningful words."}},{"n":22,"text":"रामेयं मम दौहित्री काशिराजसुता प्रभो ।\nअस्याः शृणु यथातत्त्वं कार्यं कार्यविशारद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, this is my daughter's daughter, the Kashi king's daughter, lord; hear truthfully, you skilled in affairs, what she needs done."}},{"n":23,"text":"परमं कथ्यतां चेति तां रामः प्रत्यभाषत ।\nततः साभ्यगमद्रामं ज्वलन्तमिव पावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama said to her, \"Say your supreme purpose.\" Then she approached Rama, who was like blazing fire."}},{"n":24,"text":"सा चाभिवाद्य चरणौ रामस्य शिरसा शुभा ।\nस्पृष्ट्वा पद्मदलाभाभ्यां पाणिभ्यामग्रतः स्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bowing her head to Rama's feet, that fair one touched them with hands like lotus petals and stood before him."}},{"n":25,"text":"रुरोद सा शोकवती बाष्पव्याकुललोचना ।\nप्रपेदे शरणं चैव शरण्यं भृगुनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Full of grief, her eyes dim with tears, she wept, and took refuge with the Bhrigu's son, the giver of refuge."}},{"text":"राम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Rama said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"यथासि सृञ्जयस्यास्य तथा मम नृपात्मजे ।\nब्रूहि यत्ते मनोदुःखं करिष्ये वचनं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you are to Srinjaya, so you are to me, princess; tell me the sorrow in your mind and I will do as you say."}},{"text":"अम्बोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Amba said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"भगवञ्शरणं त्वाद्य प्रपन्नास्मि महाव्रत ।\nशोकपङ्कार्णवाद्घोरादुद्धरस्व च मां विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Revered one, I take refuge in you today, you of great vows; lift me out of this terrible ocean of mud and sorrow, lord."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्याश्च दृष्ट्वा रूपं च वयश्चाभिनवं पुनः ।\nसौकुमार्यं परं चैव रामश्चिन्तापरोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her form, her fresh youth and her great delicacy, Rama became thoughtful."}},{"n":29,"text":"किमियं वक्ष्यतीत्येवं विमृशन्भृगुसत्तमः ।\nइति दध्यौ चिरं रामः कृपयाभिपरिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What will she say?\" thus pondering, the best of the Bhrigus, filled with compassion, thought for a long time."}},{"n":30,"text":"कथ्यतामिति सा भूयो रामेणोक्ता शुचिस्मिता ।\nसर्वमेव यथातत्त्वं कथयामास भार्गवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told again by Rama, \"Speak,\" the fair-smiling girl told the Bhargava everything just as it was."}},{"n":31,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा जामदग्न्यस्तु राजपुत्र्या वचस्तदा ।\nउवाच तां वरारोहां निश्चित्यार्थविनिश्चयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that princess's words, Jamadagni's son made up his mind and said to her of lovely hips:"}},{"n":32,"text":"प्रेषयिष्यामि भीष्माय कुरुश्रेष्ठाय भामिनि ।\nकरिष्यति वचो धर्म्यं श्रुत्वा मे स नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will send a message to Bhishma, the best of Kurus, good lady; hearing my words, that king will do what is right."}},{"n":33,"text":"न चेत्करिष्यति वचो मयोक्तं जाह्नवीसुतः ।\nधक्ष्याम्येनं रणे भद्रे सामात्यं शस्त्रतेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"If Jahnavi's son does not do as I say, I will burn him with his ministers by the fire of my weapons in battle, good lady."}},{"n":34,"text":"अथ वा ते मतिस्तत्र राजपुत्रि निवर्तते ।\nतावच्छाल्वपतिं वीरं योजयाम्यत्र कर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or, princess, if your mind turns away from that, I will first set the hero king of Shalva to this task."}},{"text":"अम्बोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Amba said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"विसर्जितास्मि भीष्मेण श्रुत्वैव भृगुनन्दन ।\nशाल्वराजगतं चेतो मम पूर्वं मनीषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma had released me, descendant of Bhrigu, as soon as he heard that my mind was set earlier on the king of Shalva."}},{"n":36,"text":"सौभराजमुपेत्याहमब्रुवं दुर्वचं वचः ।\nन च मां प्रत्यगृह्णात्स चारित्रपरिशङ्कितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I went to the king of Saubha and spoke hard words; but he did not accept me, suspecting my conduct."}},{"n":37,"text":"एतत्सर्वं विनिश्चित्य स्वबुद्ध्या भृगुनन्दन ।\nयदत्रौपयिकं कार्यं तच्चिन्तयितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having decided all this by your own judgment, descendant of Bhrigu, you should think what is fitting to do here."}},{"n":38,"text":"ममात्र व्यसनस्यास्य भीष्मो मूलं महाव्रतः ।\nयेनाहं वशमानीता समुत्क्षिप्य बलात्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma of the great vow is the root of this calamity of mine, by whom I was brought under his power, lifted up by force."}},{"n":39,"text":"भीष्मं जहि महाबाहो यत्कृते दुःखमीदृशम् ।\nप्राप्ताहं भृगुशार्दूल चराम्यप्रियमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kill Bhishma, mighty-armed one, on whose account I have suffered such sorrow; I wander in the worst misery, tiger of the Bhrigus."}},{"n":40,"text":"स हि लुब्धश्च मानी च जितकाशी च भार्गव ।\nतस्मात्प्रतिक्रिया कर्तुं युक्ता तस्मै त्वयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is greedy, proud and exults in victory, Bhargava; therefore, blameless one, vengeance on him is right."}},{"n":41,"text":"एष मे ह्रियमाणाया भारतेन तदा विभो ।\nअभवद्धृदि संकल्पो घातयेयं महाव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I was being carried off by the Bharata, lord, this resolve arose in my heart: let me have the great-vowed one killed."}},{"n":42,"text":"तस्मात्कामं ममाद्येमं राम संवर्तयानघ ।\nजहि भीष्मं महाबाहो यथा वृत्रं पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So fulfill my wish today, Rama, blameless one; kill Bhishma, mighty-armed one, as Purandara killed Vritra."}}]}]}